--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/micro-input/bridge.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Micro Input navigation bridge
+
+The bridge is disabled unless `MI_ZCODE_BRIDGE_CONFIG` names a private JSON file containing explicit `scopes` and an optional private `directory`. It creates a fresh capability and generation for one window renderer. Additional windows never take over an occupied socket. Renderer replacement invalidates all outstanding requests.
+
+Requests are bounded NDJSON, authenticated before metadata access, and scoped by the complete workspace/source address. Only list and exact open are allowed. The scoped Controller list reuses its v4 source index; no conversation subscription, transcript read, text search or command execution is exposed. Responses project only address, title and live status.
+
+Open rechecks the owner metadata, live attachment and exact existing workspace tab. It then selects and reads the same task in one synchronous renderer turn. Missing targets never create a workspace or choose another task. Successful readback means the renderer selected the address, not that an installed build or physical device was tested.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant MI as Micro Input
+  participant Main as Desktop main
+  participant UI as Window renderer
+  participant Host as Same Host Controller
+  MI->>Main: capability + generation + exact scope
+  Main->>Main: authenticate and authorize before forwarding
+  Main->>UI: scoped request
+  UI->>Host: scoped metadata index / getTaskMeta
+  Host-->>UI: metadata
+  UI->>UI: recheck attachment, select exact tab/task, read selection
+  UI-->>Main: projected result
+  Main-->>MI: generation-bound result
+```
